ager"},{"type":"text","text":" ensures that each action performed in the editor gets associated with a proper scene. For actions not related to scenes ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ProjectSettings"},{"type":"text","text":" edits, external resources, etc.), a separate global history is used."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The usage is mostly the same as "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/UndoRedo"},{"type":"text","text":". You create and commit actions and the manager automatically decides under-the-hood what scenes it belongs to. The scene is deduced based on the first operation in an action, using the object from the operation. The rules are as follows:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the object is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Node","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", use the currently edited scene;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the object is a built-in resource, use the scene from its path;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the object is external resource or anything else, use global history."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guessing can sometimes yield false results, so you can provide a custom context object when creating an action.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorUndoRedoManager","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is intended to be used by Godot editor plugins. You can obtain it using "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorPlugin\/getUndoRedo()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For non-editor uses or plugins that don’t need to integrate with the editor’s undo history, use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/UndoRedo"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The manager’s API is mostly the same as in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", so you can refer to its documentation for more examples. The main difference is that ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorUndoRedoManager"},{"type":"text","text":" uses object + method name for actions, instead of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Callable","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This object emits the following signals:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorUndoRedoManager\/historyChanged"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorUndoRedoManager\/versionChanged","isActive":true}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/EditorUndoRedoManager","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/editorundoredomanager"]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/EditorUndoRedoManager/addDoMethod(object:method:_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Register a method that will be called when the action is committed (i.e. the “do” action).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGod